================================================================================
Ontology-only publish + describe_ontology: unit tests and robustness fix
================================================================================

Context
-------
The ontology-only MCP publish feature (publish a domain with only an ontology,
new `describe_ontology` tool, `has_graph`-driven tool hiding) shipped with
integration-level coverage. This adds focused unit tests for the new helpers
and the MCP no-graph restriction, and hardens the ontology-detection helper
against a malformed registry row that a new test surfaced.

Changes
-------
1. src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py
   `version_document_has_ontology` now coerces any non-dict `ontology` /
   `versions[<v>]` node to "no ontology" instead of raising `AttributeError`.
   A hand-edited row like `{"ontology": "oops"}` previously crashed
   submit-for-review and the `has_graph` computation.
2. tests/units/registry/test_registry_ontology_detection.py (new)
   Unit tests for `version_document_has_ontology` (top-level + nested shapes,
   empty/malformed) and `_version_sort_key` (numeric ordering, dict rows,
   junk tolerance).
3. tests/units/registry/test_review_service.py
   `_make_svc(has_ontology=...)`; renamed `test_submit_requires_build` to
   `test_submit_requires_build_or_ontology` and added
   `test_submit_allowed_with_ontology_and_no_build` (ontology-only submit
   succeeds with no KG build).
4. tests/units/mcp/test_domain_policy_gating.py
   Extended the stub (`classes`, `ontology`, `API_V1_DOMAIN_ONTOLOGY`) and
   added the ontology-only section: every graph tool hidden on select,
   selection message flags the domain, call-time refusal for a hidden graph
   tool, `describe_ontology` allowed (structured classes + OWL), targeting a
   domain via `domain_name` without select, policy can still hide the tool,
   and a built-domain control that keeps its graph tools.

