================================================================================
Ontology Designer: persist attribute removal on section switch and navigation
================================================================================

Context
-------
In Ontology -> Designer, removing an attribute from a class (e.g. `customerid`
on `Customer`), then leaving the page (another Ontology section or a full
navigation to KG -> Explorer) and coming back, the attribute reappeared. Root
cause: an attribute edit reaches the session only through the 500 ms debounced
`syncDesignToOntology` -> `POST /ontology/save`. That pending save was cancelled
on section switch (`flushDesignLayout` cleared the timer and saved layout only)
and dropped on full page unload (only a layout beacon + a stale `save-to-uc`
fired). On return, the Designer rebuilt attributes from the never-updated
session, so the removed attribute came back.

Changes
-------
1. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
   - Added an `ontologyDirty` flag set by `scheduleAutoSave` and cleared once the
     ontology is persisted, so exit paths know a real ontology edit is pending.
   - `flushDesignLayout` (section switch) now runs the full `syncDesignToOntology`
     when `ontologyDirty`, instead of saving only the layout — the removed
     attribute is committed to the session before leaving.
   - Extracted the pure, synchronous canvas->OntologyState derivation into
     `commitDesignToOntologyState()` (reused by `syncDesignToOntology`).
   - Added `saveOntologyBeacon` on `beforeunload`/`pagehide` (registered before
     the layout beacon): rebuilds state from the canvas and fires a keepalive
     `POST /ontology/save` so a full navigation persists the edit.
   - Reset `ontologyDirty` on load completion to avoid a stale flag.

Modified files
--------------
- src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-27.log

Tests
-----
Frontend-only change (vanilla JS). `node --check` on the edited file passes.
GREEN `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 5639 passed, 305 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings.


================================================================================
Ontology Designer: stop concurrent unload writers from reverting an edit
================================================================================

Context
-------
Follow-up to the previous entry. The first fix persisted a pending Designer
edit on unload via a keepalive /ontology/save beacon, but the removed attribute
still reappeared when the user navigated within the 500 ms autosave debounce.
Root cause is a lost-update race on the file-based session: on page unload the
Designer fires THREE keepalive writes that each do a full read-modify-write of
the session — /ontology/save (the ontology beacon), /domain/design-views/
save-current (Domain.save_current_design_view → session.save()) and
/domain/save-to-uc (Domain.save_domain_to_uc → session.save()). The two layout/
registry writers load the session snapshot from BEFORE the ontology beacon's
edit and their trailing session.save() overwrites it, so the removed attribute
is written back. (Waiting >500 ms avoided the bug because the debounced save had
already committed and no concurrent /ontology/save was in flight.)

Changes
-------
1. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
   - Added `unloadOntologyFlushed`: the ontology beacon sets it when it fires
     the keepalive /ontology/save, claiming the sole session write for this
     unload.
   - `saveDesignLayoutBeacon` and `saveRegistryOnUnload` now early-return when
     `unloadOntologyFlushed` is set, so neither races the ontology beacon with a
     stale full-session snapshot. When the ontology is already clean (debounce
     had fired), both run as before. The registry re-syncs on the next section
     switch / explicit save, which run sequentially rather than racing.

Modified files
--------------
- src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-27.log

Tests
-----
Frontend-only change (vanilla JS). `node --check` on the edited file passes.
GREEN `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 5639 passed, 305 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings.


================================================================================
Allow Editors and Builders to manage data sources
================================================================================

Context
-------
Users with Databricks App `CAN_USE` and an OntoBricks Editor or Builder role
could mutate domain metadata, but the Add Data Source picker could not load
Unity Catalog catalogs or schemas because those read-only endpoints inherited
the admin-only Settings gate. This made `CAN_MANAGE` necessary for a normal
domain-authoring workflow.

Changes
-------
1. src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   Added method-aware non-admin exceptions for catalog and schema discovery,
   including the path-parameter schema route. Settings writes and SQL Warehouse
   selection remain admin-only. Documented the allow-list in the middleware
   docstring.
2. tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py
   Added regression coverage for Editor and Builder access to all data-source
   location endpoints and for continued denial of write methods.
3. documentation/deployment.md
   Documented Builder permissions, Layer 4 role table, non-admin data-source
   management, and the retained administrator boundary for shared configuration.
4. documentation/user-guide.md
   Added role guidance to the data-source mapping workflow.
5. documentation/development.md
   Updated role capabilities and `/settings` enforcement so catalog/schema
   GET allow-list is explicit.
6. documentation/api.md
   Documented which `/settings` discovery routes Editors/Builders may call.
7. documentation/get-started.md, documentation/INFO.md, README.md
   User-facing note: Add Data Source no longer requires `CAN_MANAGE`.
8. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-editor-builder-data-sources-design.md
   Recorded the approved permission-boundary design.
9. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-27-editor-builder-data-sources.md
   Recorded the test-first implementation and verification plan.

