================================================================================
Ontology Designer: removed attribute reappears — real root cause (stale copies
in design-layout views)
================================================================================

Context
-------
Definitive fix for the recurring "I remove customerid on Customer, navigate away
and back, and it is there again" bug. The two earlier attempts (unload beacon +
concurrent-writer suppression) did not fully solve it because they targeted the
wrong layer. Inspecting the live session file showed the domain stores each
entity's attribute list in TWO independent places:
  - `domain_data/ontology/classes[].dataProperties` (the authoritative ontology)
  - `domain_data/design_layout/views/<view>/entities[].properties` (a full copy
    per design view, carrying canvas metadata: id/type/isRequired/isPrimaryKey)
Removing an attribute in the shared entity panel (Model/Map) updated only the
ontology copy. On the next visit to the Designer, the canvas is rebuilt from a
design view (still 14 attrs), `commitDesignToOntologyState` re-derives config
from that canvas, and `autoGenerateOwl` persists it — overwriting the ontology
back to 14 and resurrecting the removed attribute. Confirmed via TEMP-DEBUG
logging: /ontology/save went 14 → 13 (removal) → 13 → 14 (Designer reload).

Secondary finding: `_asset_version` is computed once at server start and only
changes on a `.py` reload (uvicorn/watchfiles ignores `.js`). Editing a `.js`
file therefore leaves the cache-busting `?v=` unchanged, so the browser served
the OLD bundle and none of the earlier front-end fixes were actually loaded —
which is why "toujours le même problème" persisted across attempts.

Changes
-------
1. src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py
   - Added `Ontology._sync_design_layout_attributes()`: after `/ontology/save`
     persists the ontology, reconcile every design-view entity's `properties`
     with the matching class's `dataProperties` (by entity/attribute name).
     Survivors keep their canvas metadata, removed attributes are dropped, new
     ones are appended with defaults. This makes `/ontology/save` authoritative
     for the attribute *set* regardless of which UI path made the edit, killing
     the whole "stale view copy flows back into the ontology" class of bugs.
   - `save_ontology_config_from_editor` now calls the sync before `s.save()`.
2. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py, src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   - Removed the temporary TEMP-DEBUG diagnostic logging added while tracing the
     bug (/ontology/save, /design-views/save-current, /domain/save-to-uc).
3. tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
   - Added two regression tests: a removed attribute is dropped from design-view
     copies (survivor metadata preserved) and a newly added attribute is
     appended to them.

Modified files
--------------
- src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py
- src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
- src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-27.log

Tests
-----
GREEN `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 5668 passed, 305 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 51.48s. New regression tests in
`TestSaveOntologyConfigFromEditor` pass.

Note (existing corrupted sessions self-heal): a session whose design views were
already polluted with the stale attribute recovers on the next `/ontology/save`
after removing the attribute once more — that save now also prunes the view
copies.


================================================================================
Ontology Designer: uniform, clobber-proof session persistence (complete fix)
================================================================================

Context
-------
Final, complete fix for the recurring "a removed attribute/relationship/parent
reappears after leaving and returning to the Designer" bug, generalised to ALL
ontology characteristics per the requirement that every change persist to the
session uniformly on page change. The earlier attempts (unload beacon,
concurrent-writer suppression, attribute-only view sync) were partial because
the true root cause is a FRONTEND load-order race, not a save race.

Root cause. ``loadOntologyIntoDesigner`` has two branches: a "merge" branch that
rebuilds the canvas from the ontology (authoritative — attributes, relationships
AND inheritances) using the saved view only for positions, and a "saved-layout-
only" fallback that loads the stale view wholesale. On a full page load the
Designer could run before ``GET /ontology/load`` populated
``OntologyState.config.classes``, so it fell into the fallback, loaded a stale
view, and ``commitDesignToOntologyState`` + ``autoGenerateOwl`` serialised it
back — overwriting the just-saved ontology. Because the design view embeds
copies of attributes, relationships and inheritances, every structural edit was
at risk, not just attributes. (Secondary: ``_asset_version`` only changes on a
``.py`` reload, so pure ``.js`` edits were served stale from browser cache,
masking earlier front-end fixes.)

Changes
-------
1. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
   - Close the load-order race: ``loadOntologyIntoDesigner`` now awaits
     ``window.waitForOntologyLoaded()`` before choosing a branch, so the
     authoritative merge branch runs whenever the ontology has classes.
   - Anti-clobber guard: new ``designerContentAuthoritative`` flag (true in the
     merge / from-OntologyState branches and on any user canvas edit via
     ``scheduleAutoSave``; false in the stale-fallback branch).
     ``syncDesignToOntology`` saves layout-only and ``saveOntologyBeacon``
     no-ops when the canvas is not authoritative, so a stale visual can never be
     serialised back over the session ontology.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py
   - Generalised ``_sync_design_layout_attributes`` ->
     ``_sync_design_layout_with_ontology``: on every ``/ontology/save`` reconcile
     each view against the ontology — drop entities of deleted classes, reconcile
     surviving entities' attributes (survivors keep canvas metadata), drop
     relationships / inheritances that no longer match the ontology, and prune
     dangling visibility references. Defence-in-depth that also self-heals views
     already polluted by the bug.
3. tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
   - Added reconciliation regression tests for relationships, inheritances and
     entity deletion (plus the existing attribute add/remove tests).

Uniform flush (verified, no change needed). On section change the sidebar's
``onBeforeSectionChange`` already flushes the shared entity panel for all
sections (``checkDirtyBeforeSwitch`` -> ``saveSharedEntity`` ->
``saveConfigToSession``) and the Designer (``flushDesignLayout``); on unload
``saveOntologyBeacon`` / ``flushSharedPanelOnUnload`` persist via keepalive.
Constraints / SWRL / axioms / expressions have their own endpoints and are
preserved by ``save_ontology_config_from_editor`` — never lost on navigation.

Modified files
--------------
- src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
- src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-27.log

