`node --check` on ontology-design.js passes. GREEN
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 5672 passed, 305 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 50.78s.

Hotfix (same day). First runtime pass of ``_sync_design_layout_with_ontology``
raised ``TypeError: unhashable type: 'dict'`` on real sessions — the
``visibility.hiddenRelationships`` list holds ``{source, target}`` dicts, not
name strings — which turned every ``POST /ontology/save`` into a 500 and made
edits look lost. Fixed: visibility pruning now only touches the string lists
(``hiddenEntities`` / ``collapsedEntities``) and is type-guarded, and the whole
reconciliation is wrapped in a try/except so this defence-in-depth step can
never break the actual ontology save. Regression test seeds dict-shaped
visibility. Re-verified GREEN: 5672 passed.

================================================================================
Root-cause fix: deleted datatype attribute resurrected from properties mirror
================================================================================

Context
-------
Despite the design-view reconciliation above, removing an attribute (e.g.
`customerid` on `Customer`) in the Designer / entity panel still saw it reappear
after leaving and returning to the Ontology page. Log tracing was decisive: the
removal reached the backend (`POST /ontology/save` with 13 attributes, session
file verified at 13), yet the very next page load's `/ontology/load` returned 14
again — with no client re-save in between. The session had silently reverted.

Root cause. A class's `dataProperties` is a *derived* view. On every session
load, `DomainSession._ensure_structure` -> `Ontology.finalize_class_attributes`
-> `sync_class_data_properties` re-derives `classes[].dataProperties` from the
datatype properties declared in `config['properties']` (matched by `domain`).
That merge is additive-only. The editor removes the attribute from the class but
NOT its `DatatypeProperty` mirror in `properties`, so the mirror survives and the
next load resurrects the attribute — mutating the cached session dict back to 14.

Fix
---
1. src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py
   - New `prune_orphaned_datatype_properties(config)` — the missing inverse of
     `sync_class_data_properties`. Drops any `DatatypeProperty` / `Property`
     whose `domain` names an existing class in which the attribute is no longer
     present. Object properties, empty domains, and domains pointing to unknown
     classes are left untouched.
   - `save_ontology_config_from_editor` now calls it right after domain/range
     normalization (so the pruned list also feeds URI-based mapping cleanup and
     the persisted `properties`). This makes `/ontology/save` authoritative:
     deleting an attribute deletes its mirror, so nothing resurrects it on load.
     Self-heals sessions already polluted on the next save of that class.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
   - `test_save_drops_orphaned_datatype_property`: end-to-end — remove
     `customerid` from the class, assert its `DatatypeProperty` leaves
     `properties`, and that a subsequent `finalize_class_attributes` (the
     next-load path) does NOT resurrect it. `hasOrder` object property untouched.
   - `test_prune_orphaned_datatype_properties_keeps_valid_and_unknown`: unit
     coverage for kept-vs-pruned (valid attr, object prop, unknown/empty domain).
3. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   - Removed the temporary `TEMP-DEBUG` logging added during diagnosis on
     `/ontology/load` and `/ontology/save`.

